{
  "release": "f1437e7b41f47b41381c2f4fde84f585bc939ddf",
  "audited_main": "0bdafda8f721aaa4981c017a61b99f1122267edf",
  "sglang_production": "f3a84556e5994f2082ac043a33a36df6b8915e40",
  "facts": [
    {
      "finding": "SGLang per-tensor FP8 wrapper explicitly uses backend=cublas.",
      "source": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/78e6e9fc4dd5eecf19fd76f5393a1ae683ee83b0/python/sglang/srt/layers/quantization/fp8_utils.py#L566"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Default and explicit cuBLASLt paths both select compute32F with FAST_ACCUM=1; alpha=1 and beta=0. Algorithm differs; scale/math settings do not change between paths.",
      "source": "https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/blob/f1437e7b41f47b41381c2f4fde84f585bc939ddf/include/flashinfer/gemm/bmm_fp8.cuh"
    },
    {
      "finding": "NVIDIA documents reduced numerical accuracy from FP8 fast accumulation on Hopper. This supports variation being plausible, not correctness of every tactic.",
      "source": "https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/archive/13.0.1/cublas/index.html#cublasltmatmuldescattributes-t"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Existing native FP8 tests use cosine similarity >0.99 versus an unquantized BF16 reference; they do not promise full-model pointwise equality across tactics. Our captured-input FP32 reference is different and must not be reported as this upstream test execution.",
      "source": "https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/blob/f1437e7b41f47b41381c2f4fde84f585bc939ddf/tests/gemm/test_bmm_fp8.py#L182"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Scoped cache excludes legacy winners by design; independent tuning is expected, and both SGLang arms already use v2 candidate selection.",
      "source": "https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/blob/f1437e7b41f47b41381c2f4fde84f585bc939ddf/flashinfer/autotuner/autotuner.py#L2020"
    },
    {
      "finding": "FP8 inherits use_cuda_graph=False and use_cold_l2_cache=False. Both tested contexts leave measurement policy unspecified. Profiling therefore measures an isolated eager repeated event/global-timer window, with a delay ahead of timing, rather than full-model graph replay.",
      "source": "https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/blob/f1437e7b41f47b41381c2f4fde84f585bc939ddf/flashinfer/gemm/gemm_base.py#L2155"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Release selection uses strict minimum measured latency, without numerical verification, confidence margin, or real-serving confirmation. Dynamic activation inputs are synthesized; static weights reused.",
      "source": "https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/blob/f1437e7b41f47b41381c2f4fde84f585bc939ddf/flashinfer/autotuner/autotuner.py#L3086"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Merged #8451 provides optional near-tie confirmation and audit metadata. Default tolerance remains zero; no evidence that enabling a positive tolerance improves this workload.",
      "source": "https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/blob/0bdafda8f721aaa4981c017a61b99f1122267edf/flashinfer/autotuner/autotuner.py#L3599"
    },
    {
      "finding": "Merged #6148 uses serialized algorithm descriptors, validates native applicability, rejects legacy nondefault integer tactics, and records fallback. Absent from tested 0.7.3. The observed batch1 failure is at an exact bucket and reproduces on warm reload; no evidence attributes it to index remapping.",
      "source": "https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/commit/f5c6aa76b9bc0997c4f727f91a4c5f3af2d5fc18"
    },
    {
      "finding": "The existing SGLang accuracy test for this exact model requires GSM8K score >0.70 with 200 examples, 200 threads, and 512 max tokens. Our sequential 4-shot diagnostic is not this test.",
      "source": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/78e6e9fc4dd5eecf19fd76f5393a1ae683ee83b0/test/registered/e2e/quantization/test_modelopt_fp8.py#L55"
    }
  ],
  "decision": "No need to wait for owner input. Preserve observed parity failures but separate tactic-dependent numerical variation from cache plumbing. Use existing reference/model-quality tests plus matched-tactic graph checks. Before more selection-policy experiments, qualify stable descriptor identity/fallback on cold and fresh warm reload with merged #6148. Do not enable optional tie tolerance or change production measurement policy from source inspection alone.",
  "next_checks": [
    "Run the existing SGLang model accuracy test unchanged in opt-out and opt-in arms; retain the targeted batch-one diagnostic.",
    "Bounded native descriptor persistence check on a pinned build containing #6148: record descriptor bytes and fallback counts, eager/graph correctness, cold and fresh-process warm reuse. A fix is not automatically an integration dependency unless the qualification establishes that need.",
    "Treat any further timing as paired serving measurements over stable identities; compare matched tactics separately from independent selection."
  ],
  "execution": "Source audit and offline replay only; no new GPU allocation, performance measurements, CI trigger, PR or external comment.",
